{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n7-day store mining (2026-08-07..14) found 33 FORCE_CLOSE audit records, ~25 of them ADMINISTRATIVE closes — duplicate, obsolete, wontfix, stale-premise — where completing the described work is not the intent, so the completion verifier can never PASS them and operators reach for --force. A narrow attested-disposition path exists but is doubly scoped down: (a) class set — `close_disposition.DISPOSITION_CLASSES` = {duplicate, not_a_bug, escalated} only; (b) ticket type — close_precheck.py:64 gates the path to bugs, so an obsolete task/story/epic has NO truthful exit today. And the completion-FAIL message never mentions the path that exists: \"it offered only 'complete the work' or '[operator-attested]' — attesting would have been a FALSE claim\" (9b70). This is the single largest FORCE_CLOSE class.\n\n## Fix (extends the EXISTING --class mechanism; no new flag)\n1. Vocabulary: add obsolete (premise no longer holds; reason required), superseded (replaced by a named live ticket), wontfix (deliberate decision; reason required) to the single-sourced `CLOSE_CLASSES` (txn.py:168). Enumerated co-edits: common.schema.json#/$defs/close_class enum+description (same order), ticket_state.schema.json close_class description (:196-198), `close_disposition.DISPOSITION_CLASSES` AND `close_precheck._NON_COMPLETION_BUG_CLASSES` (both gain the three; their equality drift-guard tests/unit/test_close_disposition_attestation_738a.py:26 updated), the `transition.py` parser (existing `--class` gains the values; NO new --disposition flag), and `types.py` CloseClass.\n2. Administrative subset, single-sourced: a new frozenset `close_disposition.ADMINISTRATIVE_CLASSES = {duplicate, obsolete, superseded, wontfix}` — the classes valid on NON-BUG closes (not_a_bug/escalated stay bug-only vocabulary). Drift-guarded by a test asserting ADMINISTRATIVE_CLASSES < DISPOSITION_CLASSES and exact membership.\n3. Write-side enforcement (gate-independent — cannot be skipped by --force or a disabled completion gate): extend `txn.transition_core`'s close-class guard (txn.py:260, today `ticket_type == \"bug\"`-gated) so (a) a non-bug close MAY carry --class only from ADMINISTRATIVE_CLASSES (anything else refused naming the allowed values — the enforcement point for not_a_bug/escalated staying bug-only); (b) obsolete/wontfix REQUIRE a reason (refusal when missing) via a new `--reason <text>` transition argument persisted as `close_reason` on the close STATUS event (present-only, mirroring close_class at txn.py:287; NOT force_close_reason, which stays the --force channel). Co-edits for the new field: reducer fold `_fold_close_metadata` (reducer/_processors_status.py:49), types.py ticket-state TypedDict (:138 area), ticket_state.schema.json.\n4. Ticket-type widening of the verification skip: close_precheck.py:64's `ticket_type == \"bug\"` gate widens to (bug AND class in _NON_COMPLETION_BUG_CLASSES) OR (any type AND class in ADMINISTRATIVE_CLASSES); `_ensure_duplicate_close_is_linked` (close_precheck.py:139, called at :508) widens from duplicate-only to {duplicate, superseded} so both demand a live replacement link (existing `find_replacement`, close_disposition.py:47); the plan-review claim gate is untouched.\n5. Attestation for reason-only classes: `close_disposition.verdict()` (:92) today returns None unless find_replacement resolves a live ticket, and `decorate_manifest` (:114) signs that replacement — so obsolete/wontfix as-written would close UNSIGNED (the 738a trap). Extend: reason-only classes mint the verdict from (class + close_reason) and decorate_manifest signs a `disposition: <class> reason: <text>` line; replacement-bearing classes unchanged.\n6. Discoverability: the close refusal surface is `close_precheck`'s CommandError assembly, which HAS ticket context — it appends the applicable-class enumeration (`--class` values valid for THIS ticket_type) to the completion-FAIL/refusal message; the static COMPLETION_REMEDIATION_GUIDANCE constant stays generic (no per-ticket data in a module constant). The 9b70 incident is the RED oracle: a wontfix-shaped ticket's failure message must present a truthful exit.\n7. Migration: existing FORCE_CLOSE records stay as-is; new administrative closes should have no reason to use --force.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The three new classes appear in every single-sourced consumer — txn.CLOSE_CLASSES, common.schema.json + ticket_state.schema.json, DISPOSITION_CLASSES, _NON_COMPLETION_BUG_CLASSES, types.py CloseClass — with the 738a equality drift-guard updated; ADMINISTRATIVE_CLASSES exists in close_disposition with exact membership {duplicate, obsolete, superseded, wontfix} and a subset drift-guard test.\n- [ ] Non-bug tickets (task/story/epic fixture each) close with an administrative class without completion verification; a non-bug close with not_a_bug/escalated (or any non-administrative class) is REFUSED in txn.transition_core naming allowed values; bug closes keep today's behavior.\n- [ ] obsolete/wontfix demand --reason (write-side refusal when missing, enforced in transition_core even with the completion gate off); the reason persists as close_reason on the close event, folds via _fold_close_metadata into reduced state, and typechecks (types.py); close_reason is distinct from force_close_reason; superseded/duplicate demand a live replacement link (_ensure_duplicate_close_is_linked widened); store-event tests per class.\n- [ ] A reason-only disposition close mints a SIGNED disposition attestation whose manifest carries the class+reason line; replacement-bearing closes keep the replacement line; an unsigned close for a valid disposition is RED.\n- [ ] The close_precheck refusal/FAIL message enumerates the applicable --class values for the ticket's type; message test asserts the 9b70 wontfix scenario is offered a truthful exit; --force on an administrative-shaped close hints the disposition alternative.\n- [ ] docs (ticket-model / user-guide) document the widened path; `make lint`/`make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786745944500429001,"uuid":"6ab9eebb-b6c5-4521-88f5-06c62d20fff7"}